SSL4EO_MAPS_TODO.md

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# large model artifacts. Weights and cached predictions ARE tracked, up to GitHub's
# 100 MB per-file limit; anything above that goes to Zenodo. The only current case is
# the 461 MB full-AGBD PANGAEA checkpoint — its run config is tracked instead.
*.pth
benchmark_pangaea/full/runs/**/*.log-*

# session generator/sweep tooling (not shipped)
_launcher_tooling/

# release-assembly working doc (not shipped)
DATA_MANIFEST.md

# Bulk data fetched by the download script (see DATA_MANIFEST.md).
# The small statistics/aux .pkl and .csv under data/ ARE tracked.
data/patches/**/*.h5
data/patches/*.h5
data/patches/subsampled_indices.pkl
data/AEF/
data/weights/
data/eval_plots/

# Cached raw activations for the feature-visualisation figure, written by
# model/extract_features.py (AEF/AGBD, ~100 MB each) and model/extract_features_ssl4eo.py
# (SSL4EO, 256-d, ~200 MB each) -- both over GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit. Regenerable; kept on
# disk so re-zooming/re-colouring make_feature_figure.py is instant instead of a ~15 min model
# re-run, so delete them only if you are willing to pay that again. The '**' makes this catch the
# archive_*/ subdir too -- the old non-recursive glob missed it, which is how three archived
# *_feat.npy ended up tracked AND over the limit (see DATA_MANIFEST.md section E for the
# `git rm --cached` needed to drop them; .gitignore alone will not untrack an already-committed
# file). The small per-crop *_geo.json / *_meta.json / *_valid.npy and the s2rgb/pred GeoTIFFs
# next to them ARE tracked.
comparison/maps/features/**/*.npy

# Bulk Sentinel-2 true-colour tiles for the AGBRef comparison maps (comparison/agbref/make_plot_maps.py
# reads them from here) -- 7 JP2s, ~130 MB each, over the 100 MB limit. Provenance in
# DATA_MANIFEST.md section E.
comparison/agbref/data/s2_tci/
